AU  - Pradeep Yadav
TI  - FinTech Innovation and Alternative Financing Models for Startup Growth
PY  - 2026
AB  - The integration between FinTech and behavioral economics changes the face of startup funding by broadening the availability of funds beyond conventional banking networks. This chapter analyzes the impact of FinTech trends like AI-powered lending, equity crowdfunding, revenue-based financing, DeFi, and open banking on decision-making among entrepreneurs and investors. Utilizing ideas from prospect theory, hyperbolic discounting, herding, and nudging, this chapter creates a model that correlates behavioral biases and FinTech platform design. It demonstrates how FinTech platforms can mitigate cognitive biases that restrict startup funding options. Examples of FinTech environments worldwide in North America, Europe, Asia-Pacific, Africa, and Latin America reveal variations in FinTech adoption and regulations among regions. Further research topics for this study include algorithmic bias, cross-cultural behavioral biases, and CBDCs in startup finance.
